devHandoff.message:
Schema fix applied. Both `mood_before` and `mood_after` constraints on `thrivor_check_ins` widened from 1–5 to 1–10 (with NULL allowed). Also made them nullable since daily check-ins may not always have both.

SQL executed:
```sql
ALTER TABLE thrivor_check_ins DROP CONSTRAINT thrivor_check_ins_mood_before_check;
ALTER TABLE thrivor_check_ins ADD CONSTRAINT thrivor_check_ins_mood_before_check CHECK (mood_before IS NULL OR (mood_before >= 1 AND mood_before <= 10));
ALTER TABLE thrivor_check_ins DROP CONSTRAINT thrivor_check_ins_mood_after_check;
ALTER TABLE thrivor_check_ins ADD CONSTRAINT thrivor_check_ins_mood_after_check CHECK (mood_after IS NULL OR (mood_after >= 1 AND mood_after <= 10));
```

This is Option 1 (quick unblock). Option 2 (migrate daily check-ins to `thrivor_daily_check_ins` which already has `mood_score` 1–10 and `energy_score` 1–10) is the right long-term fix — we should ticket that separately.

You should be unblocked now. Give it a try with mood values > 5.
